    {
      "name": "Environment Setup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Instructions & Configuration",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ""
              ]
            },
            "description": "## Setup Instructions\n\n### 1. Create a Postman Environment\nBefore running any requests, you need to set up environment variables:\n\n1. Click on \"Environments\" in the left sidebar\n2. Create a new environment called \"ms-risk-engine-local\" (or any name you prefer)\n3. Add the following variables:\n   - `base_url`: http://localhost:8080 (or your server's URL)\n   - `requestId`: Will be auto-generated by pre-request scripts\n\n### 2. Select the Environment\n- In the top-right corner, select your environment from the dropdown\n\n### 3. Available Form Change Fields\nThe `formChanges` object accepts the following fields:\n- **interestRate** (number): Interest rate percentage (e.g., 5.5)\n- **termMonths** (number): Loan/mortgage term in months (e.g., 60, 360)\n- **requestedAmount** (number): Requested loan/credit amount (e.g., 25000)\n- **annualIncome** (number): Annual income of the applicant (e.g., 50000)\n- **employmentStatus** (string): Employment status (e.g., \"EMPLOYED\", \"SELF_EMPLOYED\", \"UNEMPLOYED\")\n- **hasMortgage** (boolean): Whether the customer has existing mortgage obligations (true/false)\n- **propertyValue** (number): Property value in EUR (for MORTGAGE only, needed to calculate LTV)\n\n### 4. Supported Request Types\n- **LOAN**: Standard personal/business loan\n- **MORTGAGE**: Home mortgage product\n- **CREDIT_CARD**: Credit card product\n\n### 5. Running Requests\nSelect any request from the collection and click \"Send\". The pre-request script will automatically generate a unique `requestId`.\n\n### 6. Expected Response Structure\nAll successful requests (HTTP 200) will return:\n```json\n{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-LOAN-1234567890-1234\",\n  \"partyId\": \"PARTY-123\",\n  \"baseScoringId\": \"SCORING-123\",\n  \"formChanges\": { /* your input changes */ },\n  \"simulatedResults\": {\n    \"probabilityOfDefault\": 0.05,\n    \"exposureAtDefault\": 25000,\n    \"lossGivenDefault\": 0.35,\n    \"expectedCreditLoss\": 437.5,\n    \"riskGrade\": \"A\"\n  },\n  \"delta\": {\n    \"deltaPD\": 0.01,\n    \"deltaEL\": 50.0,\n    \"deltaRiskGrade\": \"+0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 7. Troubleshooting\n\n**400 Bad Request**\n- Verify all required fields are present (requestId, requestType, formChanges)\n- Check that field values match expected types (numbers as numbers, not strings)\n- Verify requestType is one of: LOAN, MORTGAGE, CREDIT_CARD\n\n**Validation Errors**\n- Check that formChanges only contains allowed field names\n- For MORTGAGE, include propertyValue to calculate LTV\n- Verify employmentStatus matches accepted values\n\n**500 Internal Server Error**\n- Check that the ms-risk-engine service is running\n- Review the server logs for detailed error information\n- Verify database/external service connectivity"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
